# Internationalization (i18n) Conventions

## Approach

Standard Android `strings.xml` with locale qualifiers + `AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales()`.

## Supported Languages

| Language | Folder | Tag |
|----------|--------|-----|
| English (default) | `res/values/strings.xml` | `en` |
| Vietnamese | `res/values-vi/strings.xml` | `vi` |

Declared in `res/xml/locales_config.xml` and referenced by `android:localeConfig` in manifest.

## String Usage in Compose

```kotlin
Text(text = stringResource(R.string.common_search))
Text(text = stringResource(R.string.greeting, userName))
```

ALWAYS use `stringResource()` in composables. NEVER hardcode user-visible text.

## String Naming Convention

```xml
<string name="[feature]_[component]_[description]">Text</string>
```

Examples:
```xml
<string name="login_email_label">Email</string>
<string name="login_password_label">Password</string>
<string name="dm_no_messages">No messages yet</string>
<string name="message_input_placeholder">Type a message</string>
<string name="notification_channel_messages">Channel Messages</string>
<string name="common_go_back">Go back</string>
```

Prefixes:
- `common_` — shared across features
- `login_` — auth/login screen
- `dm_` — direct messages
- `message_` — chat messages
- `notification_` — notification channels/content
- `settings_` — settings screen
- `channel_list_` — channel list

## LocaleManager (DataStore persistence)

```kotlin
@Singleton
class LocaleManager @Inject constructor(
    private val dataStore: DataStore<Preferences>
) {
    val currentLanguage: Flow<String>
    suspend fun setLanguage(languageTag: String)
    suspend fun restoreOnColdStart()
}
```

Located in `session/LocaleManager.kt`. Persists language tag to DataStore.

### `restoreOnColdStart()` — called in `MainActivity.onCreate`

Only applies locale if it differs from current `AppCompatDelegate.getApplicationLocales()` — prevents redundant Activity recreation.

### `setLanguage()` — called from settings UI

Updates DataStore and immediately calls `AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales()` which triggers Activity recreation.

## Activity Recreation Handling

When locale changes, Activity is recreated. To prevent blank flash:

1. `MainActivity.onSaveInstanceState()` saves current `startDestination`
2. `onCreate()` restores it from `savedInstanceState`
3. `restoreOnColdStart()` only runs when `savedInstanceState == null` (true cold start)

## Adding a New Language

1. Create `res/values-<tag>/strings.xml` (copy from `values/strings.xml`, translate all strings)
2. Add `<locale android:name="<tag>" />` to `res/xml/locales_config.xml`
3. Add constant to `LocaleManager.SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES`
4. Add label to language picker in settings UI

## Rules

- Every user-visible string MUST be in `strings.xml` — no inline text in Kotlin/Compose
- Every string in `values/strings.xml` MUST have a translation in ALL `values-*/strings.xml`
- Use `stringResource()` in composables, `context.getString()` outside composables
- String parameters use positional format: `%1$s`, `%2$d` (not `%s`, `%d`)
- Notification channel names and descriptions MUST be in strings.xml (required by Android)
- Content descriptions for accessibility MUST be in strings.xml
